#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_1.php:11 quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_2.php:10
#, php-format
msgid "Ligatures Proofreading Tutorial, page %d"
msgstr "Anleitung für das Korrekturlesen von Ligaturen, Seite %d"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_1.php:13
msgid ""
"The two ligatures æ and œ can be difficult to distinguish when they are "
"printed italics.  However, the œ (oe) ligature is usually rounder at the "
"top, while the 'a' of æ is more teardrop-shaped.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_1.php:20
#, php-format
msgid ""
"You can insert each of these characters using the character picker in the "
"proofreading interface or using keyboard shortcuts. Tables for <a "
"href='%1$s' target='_blank'>Windows</a> and <a href='%2$s' "
"target='_blank'>Macintosh</a> which list these shortcuts are in the "
"Proofreading Guidelines."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_1.php:26 quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_2.php:18
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:31 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:35
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:29 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:25
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:17 quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:20
