#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_2.php:12
msgid ""
"In other fonts, the æ may have a little bump sticking up in the middle "
"showing the vertical line of the a:"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_aeoe_2.php:17
msgid ""
"If the word is in Latin (or derived from Latin), then there is another way "
"to distinguish these characters: Latin words often end in -æ, but never in -"
"œ."
msgstr ""
"Falls das Wort in Latein ist (oder von Latein abgeleitet), gibt es einen "
"anderen Weg diese Zeichen zu unterscheiden: Lateinische Wörter enden oft mit "
"-æ, aber niemals mit -œ."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:8
msgid "Basic Proofreading Tutorial"
msgstr "Grundlegende Korrekturlese-Anleitung"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:10 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:11
msgid "Proofreading Tutorial"
msgstr "Korrekturlese-Anleitung"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:11 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:11
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:12
msgid "Intro"
msgstr "Intro"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:12
msgid ""
"In this tutorial you will be presented extracts from the Proofreading "
"Guidelines. After each part you will be led to a quiz page, where you can "
"try out the newly learned rules."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:13
msgid ""
"Don't be alarmed by the number of changes you'll have to apply in the "
"quizzes. On normal easy texts the rate of things to correct is usually much "
"lower than that."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:15 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:10 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:10
#, php-format
msgid "Basic Proofreading Tutorial, page %d"
msgstr "Grundlegende Korrekturlese-Anleitung, Seite %d"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:17
msgid ""
"When you select a project for proofreading, the Project Page is loaded. On "
"this page there is a section called \"Project Comments\" containing "
"information specific to that project (book). <b>Read these before you start "
"proofreading pages!</b> If the Project Manager wants you to do something in "
"this book differently from the way specified in these Guidelines, that will "
"be noted here. Instructions in the Project Comments <em>override</em> the "
"rules in these Guidelines, so follow them. There may also be instructions in "
"the project comments that apply to the formatting phase, which do not apply "
"during proofreading."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:19
msgid "The Primary Rule"
msgstr "Das oberste Gebot"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:20
msgid "Don't change what the author wrote!"
msgstr "Lassen Sie den Text des Autors unverändert!"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:21
msgid ""
"The final electronic book seen by a reader, possibly many years in the "
"future, should accurately convey the intent of the author. If the author "
"spelled words oddly, we leave them spelled that way. If the author wrote "
"outrageous racist or biased statements, we leave them that way. If the "
"author put commas, superscripts, or footnotes every third word, we keep the "
"commas, superscripts, or footnotes. We are proofreaders, <b>not</b> editors."
msgstr ""
"Das fertige E-Book, das der Leser vielleicht erst in Jahrzehnten zu Gesicht "
"bekommt, soll die Absicht des Autors genau vermitteln. Hat der Autor Wörter "
"ungewöhnlich buchstabiert, so belassen wir sie in dieser Schreibweise. Hat "
"der Autor ungeheuerlich rassistische oder voreingenommene Aussagen gemacht, "
"so lassen wir sie so stehen. Hat der Autor nach jedem dritten Wort ein "
"Komma, hochgestellte Zeichen oder Fußnoten gesetzt, behalten wir die Kommas, "
"hochgestellten Zeichen und Fußnoten bei. Wir sind Korrekturleser, <b>keine</"
"b> Lektoren."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:22
msgid ""
"We do change minor typographical conventions that don't affect the sense of "
"what the author wrote."
msgstr ""
"Allerdings ändern wir weniger bedeutsame typographische Konventionen, die "
"den Sinn des Textes nicht beeinflussen."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:24
msgid "Page Headers/Page Footers"
msgstr "Kopfzeilen/Fußzeilen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:25
msgid ""
"Remove page headers and page footers, but <em>not</em> footnotes, from the "
"text."
msgstr ""
"Löschen Sie Kopf- und Fußzeilen, aber <em>nicht</em> Fußnoten, aus dem Text."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:26
msgid ""
"The page headers are normally at the top of the image and have a page number "
"opposite them. Page headers may be the same all through the book (often the "
"title of the book and the author's name), they may be the same for each "
"chapter (often the chapter number), or they may be different on each page "
"(describing the action on that page). Remove them all, regardless, including "
"the page number."
msgstr ""
"Kopfzeilen befinden sich normalerweise ganz oben auf der Seite in derselben "
"Höhe wie die Seitenzahl. Kopfzeilen können im ganzen Buch (oft der Buchtitel "
"und der Name des Autors) oder für jedes Kapitel (oft die Kapitelnummer) "
"identisch, aber auch auf jeder Seite unterschiedlich sein (mit dem Inhalt "
"der einzelnen Seite). Entfernen Sie unterschiedslos alle, einschließlich der "
"Seitenzahl."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_1.php:29
msgid ""
"Where a hyphen appears at the end of a line, join the two halves of the "
"hyphenated word back together. Remove the hyphen when you join it, unless it "
"is really a hyphenated word like well-meaning. Keep the joined word on the "
"top line, and put a line break after it to preserve the line "
"formatting&mdash;this makes it easier for volunteers in later rounds."
msgstr ""
"Wenn ein Bindestrich als Trennzeichen am Zeilenende steht, dann fügen Sie "
"die getrennten Wortteile wieder zusammen. Entfernen Sie den Bindestrich, "
"wenn Sie das Wort verbinden, wenn es sich nicht um ein Wort mit Bindestrich "
"handelt wie „well-meaning“. Siehe Bindestriche, kurze und lange "
"Gedankenstriche für Beispiele aller Arten. Lassen Sie das zusammengefügte "
"Wort in der oberen Zeile und setzen Sie danach einen Zeilenumbruch, um das "
"Zeilenformat zu erhalten &mdash; das macht es einfacher für die "
"Korrekturleser in späteren Runden."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:11
msgid "Paragraph Spacing/Indenting"
msgstr "Absatz-Abstände/Einrückung"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:12
msgid ""
"Put a blank line before the start of a paragraph, even if it starts at the "
"top of a page. You should not indent the start of the paragraph, but if it "
"is already indented don't bother removing those spaces&mdash;that can be "
"done automatically during post-processing."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:14
msgid "End-of-line Dashes"
msgstr "Gedankenstriche am Ende der Zeile"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:15
msgid ""
"As with end-of-line hyphenation, if an em-dash appears at the start or end "
"of a line of your OCR'd text, join it with the other line so that there are "
"no spaces or line breaks around it. See the examples below."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:17 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:17
msgid "Dashes"
msgstr "Gedankenstriche"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:18
msgid ""
"<i>Em-dashes &amp; long dashes</i>. These serve as <b>separators</b> between "
"words&mdash;sometimes for emphasis like this&mdash;or when a speaker gets a "
"word caught in his throat&mdash;&mdash;!"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:19
msgid ""
"Proofread these as two hyphens if the dash is as long as 2-3 letters (an "
"<i>em-dash</i>) and four hyphens if the dash is as long as 4-5 letters (a "
"<i>long dash</i>). Don't leave a space before or after, even if it looks "
"like there was a space in the original book image."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:21
msgid "Hyphens and Dashes"
msgstr "Binde- und Gedankenstriche"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:22 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:19
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_2.php:16
msgid "Original Image:"
msgstr "Original-Bild:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:23 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:23
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_2.php:20
msgid "Correctly Proofread Text:"
msgstr "Richtig Korrektur gelesener Text:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:32
msgid "End-of-page Hyphenation and Dashes"
msgstr "Worttrennung am Zeilenende und Gedankenstriche"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_2.php:33
msgid ""
"Proofread end-of-page hyphens or em-dashes by leaving the hyphen or em-dash "
"at the end of the last line, and mark it with a <kbd>*</kbd> after the "
"hyphen or dash."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:11
msgid "Chapter Headings"
msgstr "Kapitel-Überschriften"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:12
msgid "Proofread chapter headings as they appear in the image."
msgstr ""
"Lesen Sie Kapitelüberschriften so Korrektur, wie sie im Bild erscheinen."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:13
msgid ""
"A chapter heading may start a bit farther down the page than the page header "
"and won't have a page number on the same line. Chapter Headings are often "
"printed all caps; if so, keep them as all caps."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:14
msgid ""
"Watch out for a missing double quote at the start of the first paragraph, "
"which some publishers did not include or which the OCR missed due to a large "
"capital in the image. If the author started the paragraph with dialog, "
"insert the double quote."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:16
msgid "Large, Ornate opening Capital letter (Drop Cap)"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:17
msgid ""
"Proofread a large and ornate graphic first letter of a chapter, section, or "
"paragraph as if it were an ordinary letter."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:19
msgid "Period Pause \"...\" (Ellipsis)"
msgstr "Gedankenpause „...“ (Ellipse)"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:20
msgid ""
"An ellipsis should have three dots.  Regarding the spacing, in the middle of "
"a sentence treat the three dots as a single word (i.e., usually a space "
"before the 3 dots and a space after). At the end of a sentence treat the "
"ellipsis as ending punctuation, with no space before it."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:21
msgid ""
"Note that there will also be an ending punctuation mark at the end of a "
"sentence, so in the case of a period there will be 4 dots total. Remove "
"extra dots, if any, or add new ones, if necessary, to bring the number to "
"three (or four) as appropriate."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:23 quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:22
msgid "Formatting"
msgstr "Opmaken"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:24
msgid ""
"You may sometimes find formatting already present in the text. <b>Do not add "
"or correct this formatting information</b>; the formatters will do that "
"later in the process. Some examples of formatting tasks include &lt;b&gt;"
"bold&lt;/b&gt; for <b>bold</b> text."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:26
msgid "Words in Small Capitals"
msgstr "Wörter in Kapitälchen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_3.php:27
msgid ""
"Please proofread only the characters in <span style='font-variant: small-"
"caps'>Small Caps</span> (capital letters which are smaller than the standard "
"capitals). Do not worry about case changes. If the OCR'd text is already ALL-"
"CAPPED, Mixed-Cased, or lower-cased, leave it ALL-CAPPED, Mixed-Cased, or "
"lower-cased."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:12
msgid ""
"In general, a punctuation mark should have a space after it but no space "
"before it. If the OCR'd text has no space after a punctuation mark, add one; "
"if there is a space before punctuation, remove it. However, punctuation "
"marks that normally appear in pairs, such as \"quotation marks\", "
"(parentheses), [brackets], and {braces} normally have a space before the "
"opening mark, which should be retained."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:14 tools/post_proofers/ppv_report.php:383
msgid "Illustrations"
msgstr "Abbildungen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:15
msgid ""
"Ignore illustrations, but proofread any caption text as it is printed, "
"preserving the line breaks. If the caption falls in the middle of a "
"paragraph, use blank lines to set it apart from the rest of the text."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:17 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_5.php:11
msgid "Footnotes/Endnotes"
msgstr "Fußnoten/Endnoten"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:18
msgid ""
"Proofread footnotes by leaving the text of the footnote at the bottom of the "
"page and placing a tag where it is referenced in the text."
msgstr ""
"Lesen Sie Fußnoten Korrektur indem Sie den Text der Fußnote am unteren "
"Seitenrand belassen und und eine Marke dort im Text platzieren, wo sie "
"referenziert ist."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:19
msgid ""
"In the main text, the character that marks a footnote location should be "
"surrounded with square brackets (<kbd>[</kbd> and <kbd>]</kbd>) and placed "
"right next to the word being footnoted<kbd>[1]</kbd> or its punctuation mark,"
"<kbd>[2]</kbd> as shown in the image and the two examples in this sentence. "
"Footnote markers may be numbers, letters, or symbols. When footnotes are "
"marked with a symbol or a series of symbols (<kbd>*</kbd>, <kbd>†</kbd>, "
"<kbd>‡</kbd>, <kbd>§</kbd>, etc.) we replace them all with <kbd>[*]</kbd> in "
"the text, and <kbd>*</kbd> next to the footnote itself."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:20
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the page, proofread the footnote text as it is printed, "
"preserving the line breaks. Be sure to use the same tag before the footnote "
"as you used in the text where the footnote was referenced. Use just the "
"character itself for the tag, without any brackets or other punctuation."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_4.php:23
msgid ""
"You may sometimes find formatting already present in the text. <b>Do not add "
"or change this formatting information</b>; the formatters will do that later "
"in the process. Some examples of formatting tasks include &lt;i&gt;"
"italics&lt;/i&gt; for <i>italicized</i> text."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:11
msgid "Poetry/Epigrams"
msgstr "Gedichte/Epigramme"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:12
msgid ""
"Insert a blank line at the start of the poetry or epigram and another blank "
"line at the end, so that the formatters can clearly see the beginning and "
"end. Leave each line left justified and maintain the line breaks. Insert a "
"blank line between stanzas, when there is one in the image."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:14
msgid "Font size changes"
msgstr "Änderungen der Schriftgrößen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_basic_5.php:15
msgid ""
"Do not mark changes in font or font size. The formatters will take care of "
"this later in the process."
msgstr ""
"Markieren Sie keine Änderungen der Schriftart oder -größe. Die Formatierer "
"werden sich darum später im Prozess kümmern."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:10
msgid "Fraktur Proofreading Tutorial"
msgstr "Anleitung für das Korrekturlesen von Frakturschrift"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:12
msgid ""
"<b>Fraktur</b> is a particular kind of blackletter font, used principally "
"for German, but occasionally for Scandinavian languages. Modern readers "
"often find it difficult to read.  The alphabet is:"
msgstr ""
"<b>Fraktur</b> ist eine besondere Art gebrochener Schriftarten, die "
"grundsätzlich für Deutsch benutzt wurde, aber gelegentlich auch für "
"Skandinavische Sprachen. Moderne Leser finden sie oft schwierig zu lesen.  "
"Das Alphabet ist:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:14
msgid "Fraktur alphabet"
msgstr "Fraktur-Alphabet"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:16
msgid ""
"There are two different forms of the lower case letter 's'.  The "
"'normal' (or 'round') s is used at the end of a syllable, the 'long s' (ſ) "
"elsewhere. The two forms both get proofread as plain 's'."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_fraktur.php:18
#, fuzzy, php-format
msgid ""
"If you have difficulty identifying letters in fraktur, there is a <a "
"target='_blank' href='%s'>fraktur tool</a> for the fraktur alphabet."
msgstr ""
"Falls Sie Schwierigkeiten haben, die Fraktur-Schrift zu lesen, versuchen Sie "
"<a target='_blank' href='%s'>dieses Fraktur-Werkzeug</a> zu benutzen."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:9 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_5.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_2.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_4.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_5.php:8
#, php-format
msgid "Moderate Proofreading Tutorial: Part %d"
msgstr "Moderate Korrekturlese-Anleitung: Teil %d"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:12
msgid ""
"In this tutorial you will be presented extracts from the Proofreading "
"Guidelines. After each part you will be led to a quiz page, where you can "
"try out the newly learned rules. These Moderate Proofreading Quizzes build "
"on the topics already covered in the tutorial for the Basic Proofreading "
"Quiz."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:14 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:11 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_5.php:10 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_2.php:10 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_4.php:10 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_5.php:10
#, php-format
msgid "Moderate Proofreading Tutorial: Part %1$d, Page %2$d"
msgstr "Moderate Korrekturlese-Anleitung: Teil %1$d, Seite %2$d"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:16
msgid ""
"Older books often abbreviated words as contractions, and printed them as "
"superscripts. Proofread these by inserting a single caret (<kbd>^</kbd>) "
"followed by the superscripted text. If the superscript continues for more "
"than one character, then surround the text with curly braces <kbd>{</kbd> "
"and <kbd>}</kbd> as well. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_1.php:17
msgid "Superscripts example"
msgstr "Beispiel für hochgestellte Zeichen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:12
msgid ""
"Words like to-day and to-morrow that we don't commonly hyphenate now were "
"often hyphenated in the old books we are working on. Leave them hyphenated "
"the way the author did. If you're not sure if the author hyphenated it or "
"not, leave the hyphen, put an <kbd>*</kbd> after it, and join the word "
"together like this: <kbd>to-*day</kbd>. The asterisk will bring it to the "
"attention of the post-processor, who has access to all the pages and can "
"determine how the author typically wrote this word."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:14
msgid "Contractions"
msgstr "Zusammenziehungen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:15
msgid ""
"In English, remove any extra space in contractions. For example, "
"<kbd>would&nbsp;n't</kbd> should be proofread as <kbd>wouldn't</kbd> and "
"<kbd>'t&nbsp;is</kbd> as <kbd>'tis</kbd>."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:18
msgid "Dashes in Deliberately Omitted or Censored Words or Names."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_2.php:19
msgid ""
"If represented by a dash in the image, proofread these as two hyphens or "
"four hyphens as described for em-dashes &amp; long dashes. When it "
"represents a word, we leave appropriate space around it like it's really a "
"word. If it's only part of a word, then no spaces&mdash;join it with the "
"rest of the word."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:12
#, fuzzy
msgid "Non-ASCII Characters"
msgstr "Nicht-ASCII-Zeichen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:13
msgid ""
"Please proofread these using the proper UTF-8 characters. For characters "
"which are not in Unicode, see the Project Manager's instructions in the "
"Project Comments."
msgstr ""
"Bitte lesen Sie diese Korrektur, indem sie die passenden UTF-8-Zeichen "
"benutzen. Für Zeichen, die nicht in Unicode sind, siehe die Anweisungen des "
"Projekt-Managers in den Projekt-Kommentaren."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:15 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:13
msgid "Inserting Special Characters"
msgstr "Besondere Zeichen Einfügen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:16 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:14
msgid ""
"If they are not on your keyboard, there are several ways to input special "
"characters:"
msgstr ""
"Falls sie nicht auf Ihrer Tastatur sind, gibt es mehrere Wege besondere "
"Zeichen einzugeben:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:18 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:16
msgid "The character picker at the bottom of the proofreading interface."
msgstr "Die Zeichen-Auswahl am unteren Rand der Korrekturlese-Oberfläche."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:19 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:17
msgid "Keyboard shortcuts."
msgstr "Tastaturkürzel."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:21 quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:19
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Tables for <a href='%1$s' target='_blank'>Windows</a> and <a href='%2$s' "
"target='_blank'>Macintosh</a> which list these shortcuts are in the "
"Proofreading Guidelines."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:28
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Other methods described in the <a href='%s' target='_blank'>guidelines</a>."
msgstr ""
"Andere Methoden, die in den <a href='%s' target='_blank'>Richtlinien</a> "
"beschrieben sind."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:34
msgid "Fractions"
msgstr "Brüche"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_3.php:35
msgid ""
"Proofread fractions as follows: <kbd>¼</kbd> becomes <kbd>1/4</kbd>, and "
"<kbd>2½</kbd> becomes <kbd>2-1/2</kbd>. The hyphen prevents the whole and "
"fractional part from becoming separated when the lines are rewrapped during "
"post-processing."
msgstr ""
"Lesen Sie Brüche wie folgt Korrektur: aus <kbd>¼</kbd> wird <kbd>1/4</kbd>, "
"und <kbd>2½</kbd> wird zu <kbd>2-1/2</kbd>. Der Bindestrich verhindert, dass "
"die Ganzzahl und der Bruch getrennt werden, wenn die Zeilen während der "
"Nachbearbeitung neu umgebrochen werden."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:11
msgid "Common OCR Problems"
msgstr "Allgemeine OCR-Probleme"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:12
msgid ""
"OCR commonly has trouble distinguishing between the similar characters.  "
"Some examples are:"
msgstr ""
"Die OCR hat generell Probleme damit, ähnliche Zeichen zu unterscheiden. "
"Einige Beispiele sind:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:14
msgid ""
"The digit '1' (one), the lowercase letter 'l' (ell), and the uppercase "
"letter 'I'. Note that in some fonts the number one may look like <small>I</"
"small> (like a small capital letter 'i')."
msgstr ""
"Die Ziffer „1“ (eins), der Kleinbuchstabe „l“ (ell), und der Großbuchstabe "
"„I“. Beachten Sie, dass in einigen Schriftarten die Nummer eins wie ein "
"<small>I</small> (wie der kleine Großbuchstabe „i“) aussehen kann."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:15
msgid "The digit '0' (zero), and the uppercase letter 'O'."
msgstr "Die Ziffer „0“ (Null), und der Großbuchstabe „O“."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:16
msgid ""
"Dashes &amp; hyphens: Proofread these carefully&mdash;OCR'd text often has "
"only one hyphen for an em-dash that should have two."
msgstr ""
"Gedanken- & Bindestriche: Lesen Sie diese sorgfältig Korrektur &mdash; Text "
"aus der Zeichenerkennung hat oft nur einen Bindestrich für einen "
"Gedankenstrich, der zwei haben sollte."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:17
msgid "Parentheses ( ) and curly braces { }."
msgstr "Klammern ( ) und geschweifte Klammern { }."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_4.php:19
msgid ""
"Watch out for these. Normally the context of the sentence is sufficient to "
"determine which is the correct character, but be careful&mdash;often your "
"mind will automatically 'correct' these as you are reading."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_5.php:12
msgid ""
"In the main text of the page, the character that marks a footnote\n"
"    location should be surrounded with square brackets (<kbd>[</kbd> and "
"<kbd>]</kbd>)\n"
"    and placed next to the word<kbd>[*]</kbd> being footnoted or its "
"punctuation mark.<kbd>[*]</kbd>"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_5.php:15
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the page, place each footnote on a separate line in\n"
"    order of appearance, with a blank line before each one."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod1_5.php:17
msgid ""
"Do not include any horizontal lines separating the footnotes from the main "
"text."
msgstr ""
"Schließen Sie keine horizontalen Linien mit ein, welche die Fußnoten vom "
"Haupttext trennen."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:11
msgid "Paragraph Side-Descriptions (Sidenotes)"
msgstr "Absatz-Randbeschreibungen (Randnoten)"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:12
msgid ""
"Some books have short descriptions of the paragraph along the side of the "
"text. These are called sidenotes. Proofread the sidenote text as it is "
"printed, preserving the line breaks (while handling end-of-line hyphenation "
"and dashes normally)."
msgstr ""
"Manche Bücher haben kurze Beschreibungen des Abschnitts neben dem Text "
"stehen. Diese werden Randnoten genannt. Lesen Sie den Text der Randnote so "
"Korrektur, wie er gedruckt ist, und behalten die Zeilenumbrüche bei (wobei "
"Sie Binde- und Gedankenstriche wie üblich behandeln)."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:13
msgid ""
"Leave a blank line before and after the sidenote so that it can be "
"distinguished from the text around it. The OCR may place the sidenotes "
"anywhere on the page, and may even intermingle the sidenote text with the "
"rest of the text. Separate them so that the sidenote text is all together, "
"but don't worry about the position of the sidenotes on the page."
msgstr ""
"Lassen Sie eine Leerzeile vor und nach der Randnote, damit sie vom übrigen "
"Text unterschieden werden kann. Die OCR-Software kann die Randnote irgendwo "
"auf der Seite platzieren oder sie sogar mit dem übrigen Text vermischen. "
"Trennen Sie den Text so, dass der Text der Randnote zusammensteht, aber "
"kümmern Sie sich nicht um ihre Position auf der Seite."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:15
msgid "Multiple Columns"
msgstr "Mehrere Spalten"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_1.php:16
msgid ""
"Proofread ordinary text that has been printed in multiple columns as a "
"single column. Place the text from the left-most column first, the text from "
"the next column below that, and so on. Do not mark where the columns were "
"split, just join them together."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_2.php:12
msgid ""
"Subscripted text is often found in scientific works, but is not common in "
"other material. Proofread subscripted text by inserting an underline "
"character <kbd>_</kbd> and surrounding the text with curly braces <kbd>{</"
"kbd> and <kbd>}</kbd>. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_2.php:14
msgid "Subscripts example"
msgstr "Beispiel für tiefgestellte Zeichen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:11
msgid "Accented/Non-ASCII Characters"
msgstr "Akzentuierte/Nicht-ASCII-Zeichen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:12
msgid ""
"The œ character (oe ligature) should be inserted into the proofread text, "
"just like other special characters."
msgstr ""
"Das œ-Zeichen (oe-Ligatur) sollte so in den Korrektur gelesenen Text "
"eingefügt werden wie andere Sonderzeichen."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_3.php:26
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Other methods described in the guidelines: <a href='%s' "
"target='_blank'>Characters with Diacritical Marks</a> and <a href='%s' "
"target='_blank'>Inserting Special Characters</a>."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_4.php:12
msgid ""
"Proofread quotation marks at the beginning of each line of a quotation by "
"removing all of them <b>except for</b> the one at the start of the "
"quotation. If a quotation like this goes on for multiple paragraphs, leave "
"the quote mark that appears on the first line of each paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_4.php:13
msgid ""
"Often there is no closing quotation mark until the very end of the quoted "
"section of text, which may not be on the same page you are proofreading. "
"Leave it that way&mdash;do not add closing quotation marks that are not in "
"the page image."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_5.php:11
msgid "Plays: Actor Names/Stage Directions"
msgstr "Dramen: Rollennamen/Regieanweisungen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_5.php:12
msgid ""
"In dialog, treat a change in speaker as a new paragraph, with one blank line "
"before it."
msgstr ""
"Behandeln Sie einen Wechsel des Sprechers in Dialogen als einen neuen "
"Absatz, mit einer Leerzeile davor."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_mod2_5.php:13
msgid ""
"Stage directions are kept as they are in the original image, so if the stage "
"direction is on a line by itself, proofread it that way; if it is at the end "
"of a line of dialog, leave it there. Stage directions often begin with an "
"opening bracket and omit the closing bracket. This convention is retained; "
"do not close the brackets."
msgstr ""
"Regieanweisungen werden so wie im Original-Bild beibehalten; falls also die "
"Regieanweisung in einer eigenen Zeile steht , dann lesen Sie sie so "
"Korrektur; falls sie am Ende einer Dialogzeile steht, dann lassen Sie sie "
"dort. Regieanweisungen beginnen oft mit einer öffnenden Klammer und lassen "
"die schließende Klammer weg. Diese Konvention wird beibehalten; schließen "
"Sie die Klammern nicht."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:9 quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:8
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:9
msgid "Old Texts Proofreading Tutorial"
msgstr "Anleitung für das Korrekturlesen Alter Texte"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:13
#, php-format
msgid ""
"In this tutorial you will be presented extracts from the Proofreading "
"Guidelines and the %1$s Wiki article on <a href='%2$s' "
"target='_blank'>Proofing old texts</a>. After each part you will be led to a "
"quiz page, where you can try out the newly learned rules."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:15 quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:10
#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:11
#, php-format
msgid "Old Texts Proofreading Tutorial, page %d"
msgstr "Anleitung für das Korrekturlesen Alter Texte, Seite %d"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:17
msgid ""
"The fonts in older texts are generally similar to modern fonts, but one "
"major difference is in the letter s.  In older texts there are two different "
"forms of the lower-case letter s: long s and round s. The round s looks like "
"the modern letter, while the long s looks more like the letter f, except "
"that part or all of the crossbar is missing."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:18
msgid ""
"The long s is usually proofread simply as s, without marking it specially."
msgstr ""
"Das lange s wird gewöhnlich wie ein einfaches s Korrektur gelesen, ohne es "
"besonders zu markieren."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:20
msgid "Ligatures"
msgstr "Ligaturen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:21
msgid ""
"In older texts there are often flourishes connecting letters, particularly "
"the letters 'ct' and sometimes 'st'.  These are not noted specially in "
"proofreading, so just proofread them as the two letters."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:23
msgid "Single word at bottom of page"
msgstr "Einzelnes Wort am unteren Seitenrand"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:24
msgid ""
"Proofread this by deleting the word, even if it's the second half of a "
"hyphenated word."
msgstr ""
"Entfernen Sie dieses, auch wenn es die zweite Hälfte eines getrennten Wortes "
"ist."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_1.php:25
msgid ""
"In some older books, the single word at the bottom of the page (called a "
"\"catchword\", usually printed near the right margin) indicates the first "
"word on the next page of the book (called an \"incipit\"). It was used to "
"alert the printer to print the correct reverse (called \"verso\"), to make "
"it easier for printers' helpers to make up the pages prior to binding, and "
"to help the reader avoid turning over more than one page."
msgstr ""
"In einigen älteren Büchern verweist das einzelne Wort am unteren Seitenrand "
"(genannt „Kustos“, üblicherweise am rechten Rand gedruckt) auf das erste "
"Wort auf der nächsten Seite des Buches. Es half dem Drucker, die richtige "
"Rückseite (genannt „Verso“) zu drucken, und seinen Gehilfen, die Seiten für "
"das Binden vorzubereiten. Außerdem diente es als Lesehilfe, damit der Leser "
"nicht mehr als eine Seite umblätterte."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:11
msgid "Usage of u/v and i/j"
msgstr "Gebrauch von u/v und i/j"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:12
msgid ""
"In the 1600s and before, the letters <i>u</i>, <i>v</i>, <i>i</i>, and <i>j</"
"i> were used differently than they are today.  Often <i>v</i> was used only "
"at the beginning of a word, while <i>u</i> was used in the middle and end, "
"as in these words: <i>vpon</i>, <i>vntil</i>, <i>haue</i>, <i>giue</i>.  In "
"addition, usually <i>i</i> was used where we have a <i>j</i> today: "
"<i>iudge</i>, <i>obiect</i>.  The letter j may occur in Roman numerals, "
"though, such as <i>iij</i>.  In capital letters, there usually was no <i>U</"
"i> or <i>J</i>; only <i>V</i> and <i>I</i> were used."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:13
msgid ""
"Unless the Project Manager gives special instructions to the contrary, "
"proofread these just the way they appear in the image.  Do <i>not</i> "
"modernize the spelling."
msgstr ""
"Wenn der/die Projekt-Manager/in keine besonderen gegenteiligen Anweisungen "
"gibt, lesen Sie diese genau so Korrektur, wie sie im Bild erscheinen. "
"Modernisieren Sie <i>nicht</i> die Schreibweise."

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:15
msgid "Ampersands"
msgstr "Und-Zeichen"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:16
msgid "These are some examples of ampersands (&amp;) in different fonts:"
msgstr ""
"Dies sind einige Beispiele von Und-Zeichen (&amp;) in unterschiedlichen "
"Schriftarten:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_2.php:21
msgid ""
"As in many books through the 1800s, the phrase <i>et cetera</i> may be "
"abbreviated as <kbd>&amp;c.</kbd> rather than the modern <kbd>etc</kbd>.  "
"Leave it as the author wrote it."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:12
msgid "Nasal abbreviations"
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:13
msgid ""
"Sometimes an <i>n</i> or <i>m</i> is abbreviated by putting a mark over the "
"preceding letter:"
msgstr ""
"Manchmal wird ein <i>n</i> oder <i>m</i> mit einem Zeichen über dem "
"vorhergehenden Buchstaben abgekürzt:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:16
msgid "Meaning"
msgstr "Bedeutung"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:31
msgid ""
"These may be proofread as macrons <kbd>ū</kbd>, tildes <kbd>ũ</kbd>, or "
"according to the meaning (i.e. <kbd>u[n]</kbd> or <kbd>u[m]</kbd>), "
"depending on the Project Manager's instructions."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:32
msgid ""
"In a regular project, if the PM does not give any guidance, please ask in "
"the project discussion."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:35
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Inserting characters with diacritical marks, such as macron and tilde, is "
"described in the guidelines: <a href='%s' target='_blank'>Characters with "
"Diacritical Marks</a> and <a href='%s' target='_blank'>Inserting Special "
"Characters</a>."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:42
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Text like this: %1$s is in a font known as <i>blackletter</i>.  If you have "
"trouble reading it, see the wiki article on <a href='%2$s' "
"target='_blank'>Proofing blackletter</a> for images of the alphabet in that "
"font."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_old_3.php:46
msgid ""
"The hyphen in blackletter usually looks like a slanted equals sign.  Treat "
"this just like a normal hyphen, and rejoin words that are hyphenated across "
"lines.  You may need to leave hyphens as <kbd>-*</kbd> more frequently than "
"in other projects, because spelling and hyphenation in older texts is often "
"unpredictable."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_thorn.php:8 quiz/tuts/tut_p_thorn.php:10
msgid "Thorn Proofreading Tutorial"
msgstr "Korrekturlese-Anleitung für Thorn"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_thorn.php:12
#, php-format
msgid ""
"A <strong>thorn</strong> is a letter that was used in Old and Middle "
"English, and is still used in Icelandic.  It usually represents the \"th\" "
"sound.  In %s projects, it usually looks like:"
msgstr ""
"Ein <strong>Thorn</strong> ist ein Buchstabe, der in Alt- und Mittel-"
"Englisch benutzt wurde, und immer noch in Isländisch benutzt wird. Er "
"repräsentiert gewöhnlich den „th“-Klang. In %s-Projekten sieht er gewöhnlich "
"so aus:"

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_thorn.php:28
msgid ""
"The loop of the capital thorn is normally larger, and the stem may not drop "
"down as far below the line as the lower case."
msgstr ""

#: quiz/tuts/tut_p_thorn.php:29
msgid ""
"You can insert them using the character picker at the bottom of the "
"Proofreading Interface."
msgstr ""
"Sie können durch Benutzung der Zeichen-Auswahl am unteren Rand der "
"Korrekturlese-Oberfläche einfügen."

#: stats/PP_unknown.php:8
msgid "Post-Processing Mysteries"
msgstr "Nachbearbeitungs-Mysterien"

#: stats/PP_unknown.php:15
#, php-format
msgid ""
"We don't know for sure who PPd these books; if you do know, or if you did, "
"please send an email: <a href='%1$s'>%2$s</a> quoting the other information "
"in the row, including the project ID. Thanks!"
msgstr ""
"Wir wissen nicht genau, wer diese Bücher nachbearbeitet hat; falls Sie es "
"wissen, oder Sie es waren, senden Sie bitte eine E-Mail: <a "
"href='%1$s'>%2$s</a> und zitieren die anderen Informationen in der Zeile, "
"inklusive der Projekt-ID. Vielen Dank!"

#: stats/PP_unknown.php:31 tools/site_admin/manage_random_rules.php:42
msgid "Number"
msgstr "Nummer"

#: stats/PP_unknown.php:36 stats/release_queue.php:247
msgid "Date Last Modified"
msgstr "Datum der letzten Änderung"

#: stats/equilibria.php:10
